## Component Library Notes

### Thought Bubbles
Used for: preventive care reminders, approaching-period nudges, companion observations. Always dismissible with a gentle swipe. Never uses push notification patterns (no red badges, no alert styling).

### Friend State Chips
Small pill shape. Color-filled background matching the state color (low opacity). State label in Bark text. No numbers. No percentages.

### Heart Button
The send-heart button should feel physical — a slight press scale (0.92) on tap, a brief goldenrod pulse, then a soft "sent" state. Rate-limit state is communicated as a gentle opacity reduction with a tooltip, never a red error.

### Toggles
Use iOS-native toggles where possible, tinted with Moss for enabled state.

### Empty States
When a screen has no data yet (no journal entries, no workout history), the companion sits there looking curious or content. Never "No data found." Never a sad empty-box illustration. The companion *is* the empty state character.

